From 892e162fbb5326f0b01fb5ceee7951877b643ac3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 13:44:57 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 01/10] Incremental crawl: one shared delta module; big-tech
 adapters fetch details only for new, changed and aged postings

server/sources/incremental.js: change signals (rowKey), deltaPlan, runDetails, conditional
requests (ETag / Last-Modified, 304 reuse), closure probes for short lists, per-posting
accounting. Apple, Google, Microsoft/NVIDIA/Netflix (Eightfold) and Meta use it for details;
Amazon (list-only) for listing state and probes. Mapping code unchanged. polite.js: a 304 to
a conditional request is returned, not thrown (rate unchanged).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_014jaqot5Ddmi7Co6CofBiyc
